1.6
log
@whee
@
text
@Items will be pulled from this list in the order implementers feel like.

Make all databases hotsynced by default.  Requested by >1 windows users.
  - Backup bit is set when a database is created, as of a recent checkin.
    (Probably ought to add this to kMoriaUtil.prc too.)
  - Bump the preferences version number in kMoria.h.
  - At startup, where there is a preferences version check,
    if prefsVersion < 0x04,
    find each kMoriaSave-type database and set its backup bit,
    and if kMoriaColorDB exists, set its bit.
  - Don't set kMoriaDB.pdb on the fly since people may expect it to be
    read-only; set the backup bit on the copy included in the zip file
    instead.

Option for "scroll combat messages to the end".  Requested >1.
    "A toggle for "more/scroll right to the end" would be nice,
    rendering fighting against a lot of "<insertcolorhere> worm mass"
    easier, as I have to tap the display just once to attack and not
    once to attack and once to more."

Increased keyboard support.  Requested >1.
  - List the forms that still don't have full keyboard support
  - Compare implementation to documentation.. some weren't documented
  - Add missing keyboard shortcuts to implementation
  - Update documentation

Sony Clie (320x320 screen) support.  Requested >1.
  - Prerequisite: getting Sony Clie ROMs, and emulator, to debug/test.
    Downloading and reading their own funky little API.
  - Theoretically, wouldn't be too much implementation work now that
    Handera support is in.  Practically, the pain in Handera support
    was not in the implementation but in the testing, because these
    licensees' emulators do not run on Linux.  Handera needed support
    because 160x160 looks pretty stinky on 240xWhatever.  320x320 can
    do reasonable 160x160 emulation, thus there's less incentive.

"Look" mode extensions.  Requested once.
   "Perhaps the end of the list could include things that are visible
   in other directions to avoid needing to do several 'look'
   commands. It would also be useful to optionally ignore 'common'
   objects such as doors/walls/minerals etc."

Transferring a character to the desktop.  Requested >1.
  - There is a start at this in the ConvertSave directory.
    (It works on my linux machine, is untested anywhere else, and
    takes some shortcuts that it shouldn't.  It should be rewritten.)

Save the current screen state.  Requested once.
  - Font size (?? Isn't there already a Preference for font size.)
  - Stats screen (That's what he said, but is that what he meant?)

Moria emulation.  Requested once.
  - "For example, t for tunnel rather than d for dig."
  - Moria itself has two key binding modes, moria-like and rogue-like.
    kMoria does not adhere to either.  The request is to add an option
    that will make kMoria commands the same as Moria's (rogue-like
    Moria, I guess, since PalmOSish keyboards have no number pad).
  - He also requested an option to turn off the lines used in
    opening doors, spells, etc.

Verb first, then inventory list.  Requested once.
  - Add the option of capital letter commands:
    eat, read scroll, quaff = E, R, Q.  Etc.
    These should pop up an inventory screen that is filtered to the objects
    that this verb is legal for.  Hit letter to select item, hit return.

Hardware button masking for Alert forms.  Requested once.
  - Some forms don't have their own event handler, and just use a
    default handler provided by PalmOS to get a quick "yes/no" back.
    For these forms I do not currently filter out hardware button
    presses (for folks who have bound their hardware buttons).
  - I don't know if I can, without providing handlers for them and
    then having to do something silly to get the same control flow.

Jog dial support.  Requested.
  - For Handera, at least, the jog dial just puts out "normal"
    keypress events (enter, escape, prev field, next field;
    something like that) so this is morally equivalent to
    adding some keyboard shortcuts.  The question is chiefly, what
    forms could be made jogdial-navigable.
  - Document the results, or no one will ever realize it exists.
  - Antenna support (make something happen when you move antenna)
    is also requested for Palm VII :)
      It's like a hardware button: hardAntennaChr.

Improved crash recovery.
  - Save file should now be checkpointed (much) more often.
@


